<%# One partial for both views, which is the point of `template:`: the host writes
    it once and the calendar hands it the same three locals in month and in year.
    In the year view it renders inside the hover card, so it names the day too —
    the cell it hangs off is a number in a grid of twelve. %>
<% if period == :year %>
  <div class="text-xs font-semibold mb-1 whitespace-nowrap">
    <%= day.day %> <%= t('date.month_names')[day.month] %>
  </div>
<% end %>
<%# `href:` is what makes ONE EVENT clickable, and it is a different link from the
    calendar's `day_url`: that one covers the whole day cell, this one opens the
    item. In the year view this renders inside the hover card, which tippy mounts
    with `interactive: true` — the pointer can travel off the day square and into
    the card, so these links are reachable there exactly as they are in the month
    view. `Bali::Tag::Component` renders an `<a>` as soon as `href:` is present and
    a `<div>` when it is nil, so an event with no destination stays unlinked
    without the partial branching.

    `whitespace-normal h-auto py-1` is the documented opt-out from
    `tag/index.css`'s `white-space: nowrap`. The nowrap default is right for a
    table cell — #655 — and wrong here: a hover card is where the host expects to
    READ the name, and tippy caps the box at 350px. Measured before this opt-out,
    a nowrap pill holding a name of about sixty characters was 367px wide and drew
    its own background 29px past the card's right edge. `h-auto` comes with it
    because daisyUI pins `.badge` to `height: var(--size)`; wrapping without it is
    the other half of #655, where the extra lines render outside the pill. %>
<div class="flex flex-col gap-1 items-start">
  <% events&.each do |event| %>
    <%= render Bali::Tag::Component.new(
          text: event.name,
          href: event.try(:url),
          color: event.status || :primary,
          size: :sm,
          class: 'whitespace-normal h-auto py-1 text-left'
        ) %>
  <% end %>
</div>
